  <main_text>
    <l n="1">רָחַל[?], ab innocetia. Act.8.32. Plur. [Syriac plural form, illegible, ~6 letters]</l>
    <l n="2">Pasce mihi oviculas meas, Johan.21.17.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Ch.Molestum, tædiosum esse: Molestiâ, tædio</l>
    <l n="4">afficere, affligere: Item Capere, accipere, tene-</l>
    <l n="5">re, retinere, Esth.5.2. &amp; 8.15. <i>Aphel</i> Idé:</l>
    <l n="6">Et tenuerunt, Esth.4.16. in Targ. sec. Ex <i>Pahel</i> Futur.</l>
    <l n="7">Affligetis,</l>
    <l n="8">Jobi 19.2.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Ch.Postes, vectes, asferes, Esth.1.6. Asfe-</l>
    <l n="10">res proprie lecti inferiores.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Ch. Ulcísci, vindicare, Levit.19.18. <i>Ithpahel</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">Ulcísci, vindicare se, Exo.21.20. in T.H.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Ch. Ultio, vindicta.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Syr. Fossæ, foveæ, lustra, Matth.8.20.</l>
    <l n="15">Lucæ 9.58.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Ch.Percutere, contundere, cervicem confrin-</l>
    <l n="17">gere, decollare: Item Impellere, supplantare,</l>
    <l n="18">Psal.140.6. Syris est Adhærere, adjungere se alicui,</l>
    <l n="19">contrectare. Ex <i>Pahel</i> Futur. Ch. Impellet</l>
    <l n="20">eum, Psal.140.12. Syr. Adhærebant ei,</l>
    <l n="21">vel Cinxerunt, Circumdederunt eum, ut Reg. &amp;</l>
    <l n="22">Tremel. reddunt, Matth.8.1. &amp; sic idem esset, quod .</l>
    <l n="23">Ex <i>Ethpah.</i> Part. Adjun-</l>
    <l n="24">gite vos bono, ad Rom.12.9. Infinit.</l>
    <l n="25">Adjungere se, Act.9.26. Ex <i>Aphel</i> Præt.</l>
    <l n="26">Et adjunxerunt sibi, Act.17.5.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">Ch.Impulsio, Lapsus, Psal.56.14.</l>
